.TH NM 1 "July 4, 2026" "ReBSD"
.SH NAME
nm \- display symbols from ReBSD a.out object files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nm
[
.B \-gunrpo
]
[
.B \-EL
|
.B \-EB
]
[
.I file
\&...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nm
prints the symbol table from ReBSD
.B a.out
object files, executables, and archives.
If no
.I file
is specified,
.B nm
reads
.IR a.out .
.PP
For each symbol,
.B nm
prints the value, a type character, and the symbol name.
Undefined symbols are printed without an address.
When more than one file is examined, or when an archive member is printed,
the file or member name is shown before the symbols unless
.B \-o
requests one\-line prefixes.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-g
Display only external symbols.
.TP
.B \-u
Display only undefined symbols.
.TP
.B \-n
Sort symbols numerically by address instead of by name.
.TP
.B \-r
Reverse the selected sort order.
.TP
.B \-p
Do not sort; print symbols in object\-file order.
.TP
.B \-o
Precede each symbol with the file name.
.TP
.B \-EL
Read little\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.TP
.B \-EB
Read big\-endian
.B a.out
objects.
.SH SYMBOL TYPES
The type letter describes the section or class of the symbol.
Upper\-case letters are external symbols; lower\-case letters are local
symbols.
.TP
.B U
Undefined symbol.
.TP
.B A
Absolute symbol.
.TP
.B T
Text symbol.
.TP
.B D
Data symbol.
.TP
.B B
Bss symbol.
.TP
.B S
String or read\-only data symbol.
.TP
.B C
Common symbol.
.TP
.B F
Source\-file symbol.
.TP
.B W
Weak symbol.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR as (1),
.BR ld (1),
.BR ar (1),
.BR a.out (5)
